# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.frozen and tag.blocked property access; freeze/unfreeze toggle;
#         block/unblock toggle; independent flag tracking.
# defer-to: M4 (requires tag.freeze(), tag.unfreeze(), tag.block(), tag.unblock(),
#             tag.frozen, tag.blocked — all require M4 method/slot dispatch)
#
# Reason:
#   Every statement in this fixture uses a method or slot on a UTag value (frozen,
#   blocked, freeze(), unfreeze(), block(), unblock()).  These are prototype-OOP
#   dispatch operations scheduled for M4.  At M3 the UTag struct exists and
#   freeze/block flags are defined in the C struct but there is no urbiscript-level
#   method/slot dispatch surface.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with full tag method dispatch):
# # var t = Tag.new() | t.frozen;
# # [00000001] false
# # t.blocked;
# # [00000002] false
# # t.freeze(); t.frozen;
# # [00000003] true
# # t.blocked;
# # [00000004] false
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/tag/state.chk)
